MASTER WEBSITE DEVELOPMENT PROMPT — F&J WORKFORCE LIMITED

1. ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, recruitment technology architect, database engineer, and DevOps specialist. You have extensive experience building enterprise-grade recruitment platforms, applicant tracking systems (ATS), job portals, and corporate workforce websites using modern web technologies.

Build a complete, production-ready, multi-page workforce website and recruitment management platform for F&J Workforce Limited, a workforce solutions and recruitment company based in Ibeju-Lekki, Lagos State, Nigeria.

This is a real, functional web application, not a static design, landing-page prototype, or frontend-only mockup. All specified features must be implemented and connected to the backend.

2. AUDIENCE

The platform serves four primary audiences:

Job seekers: People who want to create accounts, complete professional profiles, upload CVs, discover vacancies, and apply for jobs.

Employers and corporate clients: Organizations seeking qualified workers, staffing services, recruitment support, and workforce management solutions.

Recruitment officers: Authorized F&J Workforce personnel responsible for reviewing applications, shortlisting candidates, and managing recruitment activities.

Administrators: Authorized management personnel responsible for controlling website content, services, job vacancies, registered users, applications, and platform settings.

Design the experience so that first-time visitors can immediately understand the company's services and find the appropriate action without confusion.

3. PRIMARY GOAL

Build an attractive, credible, fast, secure, and fully functional workforce website that establishes F&J Workforce Limited as a professional staffing and recruitment partner.

The website must combine:

A polished corporate website.

A multi-page services and company-information section.

A complete job vacancy portal.

