Database and storage security

Enable Row Level Security on every table exposed through the Supabase Data API.

Policies must enforce:

Candidates can read and update only their own permitted profile information.

Candidates can create applications only for themselves.

Candidates can view only their own application records.

Candidates cannot edit administrative application statuses.

Public users can read only published, eligible vacancies and public service content.

Contact and employer enquiries cannot be publicly listed or read.

Recruiter access is restricted to explicitly authorized recruitment functions.

Administrator privileges are verified through a secure, trusted role mechanism.

Unauthorized users cannot read CVs or internal notes.

Use private Supabase Storage buckets for CVs and sensitive documents. Enforce file size and type restrictions, authorize uploads and downloads, and use short-lived signed URLs where appropriate.

Do not trust a client-supplied user ID, role, status, or record ownership field. Enforce authorization on the server and in database policies.

